{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are generally below realized prices by ~0.5–2.5 EUR, especially during rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift (larger in the first ~20 forecast days).",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: after an upswing begins, the model follows with delay and insufficient slope. Add a trend-following adjustment proportional to the last 5–10 day momentum (positive momentum => boost the next 1–15 days).",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: errors grow with horizon; the back end (days ~20–30) is often too low and sometimes points to a decline that doesn’t occur. Flatten negative late-horizon slopes; pull days 20–30 toward the mid-horizon level.",
    "Missed volatility bursts: model underestimates post-breakout jumps (e.g., transitions into 68–70). If price breaks above recent 20–30d range, add a breakout premium for the next ~5–10 days.",
    "Occasional overshoot on late-horizon peaks: in some cases the model projects exaggerated highs near the end (e.g., day ~28–30 in Example 3). Cap late-horizon upside by anchoring to a smoothed trend + volatility band rather than extrapolating acceleration."
  ]
}
